timeline
    title Post-2022 developments in cardiomyocyte MEA analysis methodology
    2022 : Cardio PyMEA — open-source Python pipeline (Dunham et al.)
         : DatAnalyzer — MATLAB tool with morphology-aware FPD (own work; method in Mäki 2023, not peer reviewed)
    2023 : hiPSC-CMs as electrophysiological models — opportunities and challenges (Ismaili et al.)
         : 3D spheroid geometry as FP variability source (Hwang et al.)
    2024 : CardioMEA platform — scalable open analysis (Lee et al.)
         : T-wave peak correlates with APD90 for biphasic T-waves, in NRVM (Ernault et al.)
         : Temporal and spatial confounders quantified (Guerrelli et al.)
         : KCNH2 mutation phenotyping in 3D tissues (Maurissen et al.)
         : Functional, metabolic and transcriptional maturation largely independent (Fetterman et al.)
         : Maturation medium improves in vitro-to-in vivo translatability (Correia et al.)
    2025 : Ultra-high-density MEA field potential imaging (Matsuda et al.)
         : Healthy vs. long QT hiPSC-CM CiPA drug comparison (Park et al.)
         : Video-based interpretable-AI maturity classifier (Scheurer et al.)
         : MEA parameters differ between maturation conditions (Li et al.)
    2026 : In silico model of hiPSC-CM tissue coupled to MEA electrodes (Botti et al.)
         : PhysioMEA — cardiac organoid beat rate variability and 2D heatmaps (Weiser-Bitoun et al.)
         : CardioScripts — combined atomic force microscopy and MEA electromechanical analysis (Kabanov et al.)
         : Stacking ensemble machine learning for TdP risk prediction (Pramudito et al.)
         : Transparent MEA with FP and optical readouts of hiPSC-CMs (Lee et al.)
